Corrected 2026-08-02 for upstream linux-next context.

The original patch anchored its Kconfig hunk on `endmenu` after QCOM_PBS.
Upstream restructured drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig so that block now ends with
`endif`, so the hunk failed to apply. Same insertion point, new anchor.

Apply with:
  cp kernel/soccp_glink.c <tree>/drivers/soc/qcom/
  git apply patches/glymur-soccp-glink-7.2-hooks.patch.fixed
  ./scripts/config --module CONFIG_QCOM_SOCCP_GLINK

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -292,6 +292,14 @@
 	  This module provides the APIs to the client drivers that wants to send the
 	  PBS trigger event to the PBS RAM.
 
+config QCOM_SOCCP_GLINK
+	tristate "Qualcomm SOCCP GLINK Edge (Asus Zenbook)"
+	depends on QCOM_SMEM && RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK_SMEM
+	help
+	  Stand-alone registrar for the SOCCP GLINK-over-SMEM edge on
+	  the ASUS Zenbook A16 (Snapdragon X2 Elite). This is required
+	  to receive battery and charger status over PMIC-GLINK.
+
 endif
